# Review routing.
#
# INTERIM: everything routes to @oscarmiza, because the process-type domain
# teams do not exist yet.
#
# The intended shape is one owner per domain - the platform team owns the
# engine, each domain owns its own automations - which is what keeps review
# from becoming a central bottleneck once there are 100+ automations in the
# tree. The paths below are already split along those lines, so handing a
# domain over is a one-word change on one line rather than a restructuring.
# Adding a domain means adding a line; see "Where code goes" in AGENTS.md.

# Catch-all first, so no path is ever unowned. More specific rules below win.
*                               @oscarmiza

# ---- Core: the platform team's remit ----
/packages/                      @oscarmiza
/tooling/                       @oscarmiza
/config/                        @oscarmiza
/templates/                     @oscarmiza
/pnpm-workspace.yaml            @oscarmiza
/tsconfig.json                  @oscarmiza
/Dockerfile                     @oscarmiza
/docker-compose.yml             @oscarmiza

# ---- Automations: one entry per process-type domain ----
/automations/group-submission/  @oscarmiza
/automations/member-submission/ @oscarmiza
